{"actor":"agent:claude-code_2-1-329_agent","id":"basicly-qpr2xmr.7#ev-b2499d0e45","kind":"created","payload":{"acceptance_criteria":"A requirements comment on basicly-qpr2xmr names each dispatch outcome, states that a dispatch result never rejects and carries a stop reason, and lists the cause codes of the blocked state.\nThe comment cites concepts B1 and B17 of docs/research/deepseek-harness-plugin-review.md.","description":"## Context\nDeepseek concepts B1 and B17 (docs/research/deepseek-harness-plugin-review.md, disposition adapt): a dispatch result that never rejects and carries a stop reason, and a cause code on the single blocked state. The tracker has one blocked status with no cause code. The shape belongs in the dispatch interface of the meta harness adapters (requirement R1). Placed on this epic with no child record (docs/research/meta-harness.md, Section C). Filed on Orchestrator order 2026-11-20.","issue_type":"task","priority":2,"shaped_under":"dor.v3","title":"Define the dispatch outcome vocabulary with a cause code for a blocked state"},"record":"basicly-qpr2xmr.7","seq":1,"totals":{"attempts":0,"events":1,"spend_micros":0,"status":null},"ts":"2026-11-20T07:43:28.699420Z"}
